#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asinh

#% text
# `asinh(z)` gives the inverse hyperbolic sine.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For complex `z` the principal value is `log(z + sqrt(z^2 + 1))`.

#% item
# Exact special values and odd symmetry are applied; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asinh(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
asinh(0.5)
#% output
#= 0.48121182505960347

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
asinh(2.0*im)
#% output
#= complex(1.3169578969248168, 1.5707963267948966)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(asinh(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 0.327450150237258443322535259988258

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `atan`, `asin`, `acos`
